gitohashi: cancel dump_cb sul at PROTOCOL_DESTROY, fixes F-002

From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>

The 1s dump_cb reschedule was never cancelled when the protocol
instance was destroyed; a vhost destroyed while its context keeps
servicing (plugin embedding case) would fire the sul on freed vhd
memory and keep rescheduling.  Cancel it first thing at destroy.
---
 src/protocol_gitohashi.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/protocol_gitohashi.c b/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
index a200401..619ecbc 100644
--- a/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
+++ b/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
@@ -455,6 +455,12 @@ callback_gitohashi(struct lws *wsi, enum lws_callback_reasons reason,
 			lwsl_err("%s: NULL vhd\n", __func__);
 			break;;
 		}
+		/*
+		 * the vhd is going away with the vhost... stop the 1s
+		 * dump_cb reschedule cycle or it will fire on freed memory
+		 * if the context outlives the vhost (plugin case)
+		 */
+		lws_sul_cancel(&vhd->sul);
 		/*
 		 * A worker still inside jg2_ctx_fill() is walking
 		 * ctx->vhost, and the threadpool done-queue reap destroys
